       fhir:ElementDefinition.definition [ fhir:value "Identifies the conditions/problems/concerns/diagnoses/etc. whose management and/or mitigation are handled by this plan." ] ;
       fhir:ElementDefinition.comment [ fhir:value "When the diagnosis is related to an allergy or intolerance, the Condition and AllergyIntolerance resources can both be used. However, to be actionable for decision support, using Condition alone is not sufficient as the allergy or intolerance condition needs to be represented as an AllergyIntolerance." ] ;
       fhir:ElementDefinition.requirements [ fhir:value "Links plan to the conditions it manages.  The element can identify risks addressed by the plan as well as active conditions.  (The Condition resource can include things like \"at risk for hypertension\" or \"fall risk\".)  Also scopes plans - multiple plans may exist addressing different concerns." ] ;
